**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** The instrument-matrix condition number for choosing the polarizer and compensator states (001 §M 'the instrument-matrix condition number for choosing polarizer and compensator states'; the S14.2 brief). A state generator of the kit's polarizer followed by its compensator turned to θ makes the Stokes state s(θ) = M_C(θ) · M_P(0) · (1, 0, 0, 0); the analyzer, the same pair in reverse, reads the row a(θ), row 0 of M_P(0) · M_C(θ); a reading at generator angle θ_g and analyzer angle θ_a is the design row `MuellerReconstruction.designRow (s θ_g) (a θ_a)` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:designRow`, the row the linear engine solves, step 388), so the instrument matrix of four generator and four analyzer states is the 16 × 16 stack of those rows, and its condition number (`MuellerInverse.fs:conditionNumber`) is how much it amplifies reading noise into the reconstructed Mueller matrix. The four angles are the set, from the grid 0°, 15°, …, 165°, whose 4 × 4 generator matrix has the least condition number (a regular tetrahedron on the Poincaré sphere reaches √3), the analyzer turned to the same four; the grid is a constant of the planner. Each optic is evaluated by the one item evaluator (`ItemModelChoice.boundWith`, step 251, at `ParameterValues.ofParameters item.parameters`, step 245; `BoundOpticalElement.muellerAt` at `ElementOrientation.transmittingAt θ`, step 247) at the first source's wavelength. A compound optic (a circular polarizer, step 210) turns as one piece, so it generates states of one ellipticity and cannot complete a basis; it is not paired. In `MeasurementPlanner.fs`, after step 482's declarations. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S14.2; every case name has two words; no `bool` appears. (1) `PlannerError` gains `InstrumentEvaluationErr` (`an optic of the kit cannot be evaluated: <reason>`). (2) `InstrumentChoice = { polarizer : PlannerOptic; compensator : PlannerOptic; angles : Angle list; condition : ConditionNumber }`. (3) `InstrumentFinding` = `ConditionedInstrumentFinding of InstrumentChoice` | `CompensatorMissingFinding of PlannerOptic`, with `member this.text : string`: `<the polarizer's label> with <the compensator's label> at <the four angles in degrees, one decimal, joined by ", ">°: the instrument matrix's condition number is <κ, two decimals>.` and `<the polarizer's label> has no compensator to pair: it generates linear states only, so a full Mueller matrix needs a retarder.`, under `CultureInfo.InvariantCulture`. (4) `type PlannerInputs with member this.instrumentFindingsWith (items : Item list) (choiceOf : Item -> ItemModelChoice option) (materials : MaterialProxy) : Result<InstrumentFinding list, PlannerError>`: none without a source; otherwise, for each `PolarizerOptic` of `this.lab.optics` in order, one `ConditionedInstrumentFinding` per `CompensatorOptic` in order — the four grid angles of least generator condition, a tie keeping the earliest set in the grid's lexicographic order, and the condition of the instrument matrix built over them — or, when the lab holds no compensator, one `CompensatorMissingFinding` of it. An optic's item missing from `items`, a `choiceOf` answering `None` or an `ItemEvaluationError` answers `InstrumentEvaluationErr` naming the item's label and the cause. No cache or option is added. Tests, in `PlannerInputsTests`, over step 470's items (LP1 the linear-polarizer preset, RET the retarder plate at its quarter-wave default, step 208): `a polarizer and a retarder give the four compensator angles of least generator condition, and the instrument's condition follows`: with Laser, LP1 and RET the answer is one `ConditionedInstrumentFinding` of LP1 with RET whose four angles are distinct grid angles at which the generator matrix's condition, computed in the test through the same evaluator and `conditionNumber`, is no greater than at any other four of the grid's twelve angles (all 495 sets checked), and whose instrument condition is finite and at least 3 (a Kronecker product's condition is its factors' product, each at least √3); its text names both labels and the four angles. `a polarizer alone is told it needs a compensator, and a compound optic is not paired`: with Laser and LP1, or Laser, LP1 and CPL1, the answer is `[ CompensatorMissingFinding LP1 ]` with its text; with no source it is empty. `an optic the library does not resolve refuses the instrument findings, naming it`: a `choiceOf` answering `None` for RET answers `InstrumentEvaluationErr` naming `RET`. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved.

**Acceptance.** After the instrument findings land, `PlannerInputs.instrumentFindingsWith` MUST pair each polarizer with each compensator at the four grid angles of least generator condition and report the instrument matrix's condition, tell a polarizer with no compensator that it needs one, leave compound optics unpaired and refuse an unresolved optic; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a polarizer and a retarder give the four compensator angles of least generator condition, and the instrument's condition follows`, `a polarizer alone is told it needs a compensator, and a compound optic is not paired` and `an optic the library does not resolve refuses the instrument findings, naming it`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s46 invariants MUST pass.
